$$
\dfrac {15} {24} =  \dfrac {15\div 3} {24\div 3} = \dfrac{5}{8}
$$"] ["question-73f358ee-4606-5152-af8b-f23b8667b4f2" :question/id #uuid "73f358ee-4606-5152-af8b-f23b8667b4f2"] ["question-73f358ee-4606-5152-af8b-f23b8667b4f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-56834"] ["question-73f358ee-4606-5152-af8b-f23b8667b4f2" :question/problem "$\frac{1}{4}\times \frac{5}{6}=$"] ["question-73f358ee-4606-5152-af8b-f23b8667b4f2" :question/worked-solution "To multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:

